#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:27
msgid ""
"This package supports the `usage-pure`, `usage-global`, and `entry-"
"global` methods. When `entry-global` is used, it replaces imports to "
"`core-js`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:30
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:32
msgid ""
"See [here](../../docs/usage.md#options) for a list of options supported "
"by every polyfill provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:34
msgid "`version`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:36
msgid "`string`, defaults to `\"3.0\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:38
msgid ""
"This option only has an effect when used alongside `\"method\": \"usage-"
"global\"` or `\"method\": \"usage-pure\"`. It is recommended to specify "
"the minor version you are using as `core-js@3.0` may not include "
"polyfills for the latest features. If you are bundling an app, you can "
"provide the version directly from your node modules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:52
msgid ""
"If you are a library author, specify a reasonably modern `core-js` "
"version in your `package.json` and provide the plugin the minimal "
"supported version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:74
msgid "`proposals`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:76
msgid "`boolean`, defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3_README.md:78
msgid ""
"This option only has an effect when used alongside `\"method\": \"usage-"
"global\"` or `\"method\": \"usage-pure\"`. When `proposals` are `true`, "
"any ES proposal supported by core-js will be polyfilled as well."
msgstr ""

